# Both spellings, and the bare one is the load-bearing half. A trailing slash
# matches a *directory* only, so in a git worktree — where `node_modules` is a
# symlink up to the parent checkout — the slashed form below does not match it
# and `git add -A` tracks a 120000 blob reading `../../../node_modules`. Merged,
# every clone and every CI runner gets a dangling path where the dependency tree
# belongs. Inherited from seekolous, where it had already been committed once.
node_modules
node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.DS_Store
.vite/
.scratch/
.pi/

# probe output: regenerated by scripts/shot-*.mjs, never reviewed as source
probe-shots/

# The canonical view set (#104): PNGs and the sheet built from them. Regenerated
# by `npm run views`, and deliberately not committed — a baseline in git would
# make drift visible for free, at the price of a binary-heavy diff on every
# visual PR and a repo that grows with each lever. Before/after is two runs at
# two refs instead, which costs nothing and keeps the pair honest.
view-set/

# Claude Code scratch: agent worktrees are checkouts, not content.
.claude/worktrees/
.worktrees/

# Claude Code: the shared allowlist is tracked so a fresh worktree gets it;
# per-machine preferences are not.
.claude/settings.local.json
